     "figure_id": "F1",
     "general_description": "Line chart of serum ferritin in ng/mL for five patients A to E at nine time points from 1 year before to 2 years after the transition to RBCX.",
     "detailed_description": "Title-less line chart on a white background with a vertical grid of nine columns. The y axis is labelled Serum ferritin (ng/mL) with ticks from 0 to 8000 in steps of 1000; the x axis is labelled Time pre- and post-transition to RBCX with nine categories: 1 year pre, 9 months pre, 6 months pre, 3 months pre, 3 months post, 6 months post, 9 months post, 1 year post, 2 years post. A legend headed Patient Key at the upper right lists five series: A dark blue line with diamonds, B orange-brown with squares, C grey with triangles, D orange with x markers, E light blue with star-x markers. Patient A starts highest near 7,000 and stays above 5,600 through 3 months pre, then falls to about 2,300 at 3 months post and about 600 to 700 by 9 months to 1 year post, rising to about 1,150 at 2 years post. Patient E rises from about 2,100 to about 3,400 at 9 months pre then declines to about 500 to 550 at 1 year post and about 900 at 2 years post. Patient D rises to about 3,200 at 3 months pre, falls to about 2,300, rises to about 3,050 at 6 months post, then falls to about 1,100 at 2 years post. Patients B and C stay between about 700 and 1,400 throughout, with B ending near 700 and C near 700.",
